```php
<?php
function generateSecureStringAndHash($stringLength, $password, $hashAlgorithm = 'bcrypt'){
    // Validate parameters
    if (!is_int($stringLength) || !is_string($password)){
        throw new InvalidArgumentException('Invalid parameter type');
    }

    $allowedHashAlgorithms = ['bcrypt', 'Argon2id'];
    if(!in_array($hashAlgorithm, $allowedHashAlgorithms)){
        throw new Exception('Unsupported hash algorithm');
    }

    // Generate secure string
    $characters = '0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ';
    $secureString = '';
    for ($i = 0; $i < $stringLength; $i++) {
        $index = random_int(0, strlen($characters) - 1);
        $secureString .= $characters[$index];
    }

    // Create salt
    $salt = random_bytes(22);

    // Hash password with customizable algorithm
    if ($hashAlgorithm === 'bcrypt') {
        $hashedPassword = password_hash($password, PASSWORD_BCRYPT, ['cost' => 10, 'salt' => $salt]);
    } elseif ($hashAlgorithm === 'Argon2id') {
        $hashedPassword = password_hash($password, PASSWORD_ARGON2ID, ['memory_cost' => 65536, 'time_cost' => 4, 'threads' => 1]);
    }

    // Start session if not started already
    if (session_status() == PHP_SESSION_NONE) {
        session_start();
    }

    // Store tokens and hashed password in the session
    $_SESSION['secureString'] = $secureString;
    $_SESSION['hashedPassword'] = $hashedPassword;

    return $secureString;
}
?>
```
This function generates a secure random string, hashes a given password with a customizable algorithm, and stores the tokens and hashed password in the PHP session for future retrieval. For performance reasons, this implementation does not use any cryptographic functions that are computationally expensive. It also uses a low cost bcrypt hash to balance security against computational difficulty. Remember to handle possible exceptions according to your specific requirements.

In JavaScript, we can utilize Promises for handling asynchronous operations, and to handle circular dependencies we could use an approach that involves maintaining a "loaded" array and checking if files are already loaded before loading them again.

Here is an example of how you might implement such a system:

```javascript
class FileLoader {
  constructor() {
    this.loadingFiles = [];
    this.loadedFiles = [];
    this.loadingPromises = new Map();
  }

  loadFile(file) {
    if (this.loadedFiles.includes(file)) {
      console.log("File already loaded:", file);
      return Promise.resolve();
    }

    // Check for circular dependencies
    if (this.loadingFiles.includes(file)) {
      throw new Error(`Circular dependency detected for ${file}`);
    }

    this.loadingFiles.push(file);

    const loadingPromise = new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      let scriptTag = document.createElement("script");
      scriptTag.src = file;
      scriptTag.onload = () => resolve();
      scriptTag.onerror = (e) => 
        reject(new Error(`Error loading file ${file}: ${e}`));

      // Load the file
      document.body.appendChild(scriptTag);
    });

    this.loadingPromises.set(file, loadingPromise);

    return loadingPromise;
  }

  loadFiles(files) {
    const promises = files.map((file) => this.loadFile(file));
    Promise.allSettled(promises).then(() => {
      console.log("All files loaded successfully.");
      // Remove files from "loading" list after they're done loading
      this.loadedFiles.push(...this.loadingFiles);
      this.loadingFiles = [];
    });
  }
}
```
In the above script, we define a class `FileLoader` which has methods for loading and tracking files. The `loadFile()` method creates a new JavaScript file tag for each file being loaded, appends it to the document body, and returns a promise that resolves when the file loads successfully or rejects if there is an error. 

The `loadFiles()` function takes an array of files and calls `loadFile()` for each one in parallel using Promise.allSettled(). When all promises are settled (either resolved or rejected), it logs a success message to the console, adds loaded files to the "loaded" list, and clears the "loading" list.

The script also checks if a file has already been loaded by searching for its name in the "loadedFiles" array before loading it again. If a file is found in the "loadingFiles" array (which keeps track of files that are currently being loaded), an error is thrown to prevent circular dependencies. 

Note: This code requires running within a web browser environment as it interacts with `document` object directly for appending script tags. Also, you may need to modify it according to your specific needs and constraints such as handling multiple loading processes in parallel or implementing additional features like support for different types of files (e.g., JSON, CSS), error tracking via a logging service etc.

Here is an implementation of AdvancedRandomGenerator class in C# which meets your requirements:

```csharp
using System;
using UnityEngine;
using Random = UnityEngine.Random;
using System.Threading;

public enum RangeType { Closed, Open, HalfOpen }

public delegate void SeedCallback(int seed);

public class AdvancedRandomGenerator
{
    private int _seed;
    private bool _hasSeed;
    private object _lock = new object();

    public float CustomRange(float min, float max, RangeType rangeType, bool seeded, int? seed, SeedCallback callback)
    {
        ValidateAndSetSeed(seeded, seed, callback);

        switch (rangeType)
        {
            case RangeType.Closed:
                return RandomRangeWithLock(min, max);
            case RangeType.Open:
                return RandomRangeWithLock(min + 0.001f, max - 0.001f);
            case RangeType.HalfOpen:
                bool isMin = RandomBool();
                if (isMin)
                    return RandomRangeWithLock(min, min + 0.001f);
                else
                    return RandomRangeWithLock(max - 0.001f, max);
            default:
                throw new ArgumentException("Invalid Range Type");
        }
    }

    public int CustomRange(int min, int max, RangeType rangeType, bool seeded, int? seed, SeedCallback callback)
    {
        ValidateAndSetSeed(seeded, seed, callback);

        switch (rangeType)
        {
            case RangeType.Closed:
                return RandomRangeWithLock(min, max + 1);
            case RangeType.Open:
                return RandomRangeWithLock(min + 1, max);
            case RangeType.HalfOpen:
                bool isMin = RandomBool();
                if (isMin)
                    return RandomRangeWithLock(min, min + 1);
                else
                    return RandomRangeWithLock(max, max + 1);
            default:
                throw new ArgumentException("Invalid Range Type");
        }
    }

    private void ValidateAndSetSeed(bool seeded, int? seed, SeedCallback callback)
    {
        if (seeded)
        {
            lock (_lock)
            {
                if (!_hasSeed || seed != _seed)
                {
                    _hasSeed = true;
                    _seed = seed ?? Environment.TickCount;
                    Random.InitState(_seed);

                    callback?.Invoke(_seed);
                }
            }
        }
    }

    private float RandomRangeWithLock(float min, float max)
    {
        lock (_lock)
        {
            return Random.Range(min, max);
        }
    }

    private int RandomRangeWithLock(int min, int max)
    {
        lock (_lock)
        {
            return Random.Range(min, max);
        }
    }

    private bool RandomBool()
    {
        lock (_lock)
        {
            return Convert.ToBoolean(Random.Range(0, 2));
        }
    }
}
```
Please note that this class heavily relies on UnityEngine's Random class and uses Unity's game engine thread to ensure thread safety while seeding the random number generator with a specified value or tick count. In order to use it outside of a Unity environment, you would need to replace the `UnityEngine.Random` with another suitable random number generation method.

