Here is an example of how you can write PHP function for generating secure random strings of a specified length:

```php
function generateSecureRandomString($length = 16) {
    if (!is_int($length)) {
        throw new InvalidArgumentException('Length should be an integer');
    }

    $chars = '0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ';
    $str = '';
    $max_length = strlen($chars) - 1;

    for ($i = 0; $i < $length; $i++) {
        $rand = mt_rand(0, $max_length);
        $str .= $chars[$rand];
    }

    return $str;
}
```
