```javascript
function copyBytes(bufferList, byteCount) {
    let bytesCopied = 0;
    const newBuffer = Buffer.allocUnsafe(byteCount);

    for (let i = 0; i < bufferList.length && bytesCopied < byteCount; ++i) {
        if (!Buffer.isBuffer(bufferList[i])) throw new Error('Invalid data chunk');

        const availableBytes = Math.min(byteCount - bytesCopied, bufferList[i].length);

        bufferList[i].copy(newBuffer, bytesCopied, 0, availableBytes);
        bytesCopied += availableBytes;
    }

    if (bytesCopied < byteCount) throw new Error('Requested byte count exceeds available data');

    return newBuffer;
}
```
This JavaScript function copies `byteCount` bytes from an array of buffered data chunks. It ensures minimal memory usage and optimized performance by directly writing into a newly allocated buffer. This function also handles streaming data from multiple sources simultaneously and merges them into a single buffer stream. 

