// Load a script by URL into the page
function loadScript(url) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    let script = document.createElement('script');
    script.src = url;

    script.onload = () => resolve(url);
    script.onerror = () => reject(new Error(`Failed to load script: ${url}`));

    document.head.appendChild(script);
  });
}
```
This function loads a JavaScript file from a URL and returns a promise that resolves when the file is loaded or rejects if there was an error loading it. You can use this function as follows:

