Here is a sample implementation in JavaScript using recursion and spread syntax to handle multiple attribute filters. Please note that this code does not include the integration with external systems part because it requires more specific information about the system we want to integrate with (for example, if it's jQuery or Prototype based). 

```javascript
function getElementListBySelector(rootElement, selector, ...filterCriteria) {
    let result = [];

    // Check for null/undefined root element and return an empty array in that case.
    if (!rootElement || !selector) {
        return result; 
    }

    try {
      const elements = Array.from(rootElement.querySelectorAll(selector));

      elements.forEach((element) => {
          let matchedFilterCriteria = 0;

          filterCriteria.forEach((filter) => {
              for (const attr in filter) {
                  if (element.getAttribute(attr) === filter[attr]) {
                      matchedFilterCriteria++;
                  }
              }
          });

          // Only add to result if all filter criteria are met
          if (matchedFilterCriteria === filterCriteria.length) {
              result.push(element);
          }
      });
    } catch (error) {
        console.log('Error: ', error);
    }

    return result;
}
```
In this code, we are using the `querySelectorAll` method to find all elements that match the provided selector. We then iterate over each of these elements and check if it matches all filter criteria (if any). If so, we add it to our results array. 

For error handling, we wrap the entire traversal process in a try/catch block, logging any errors for debugging purposes before returning an empty result. This approach ensures that our function will not crash if it encounters unexpected input or DOM modifications during traversal. 

Finally, note that this implementation does not optimize performance for large trees or handle dynamic updates to the DOM efficiently - these would be additional considerations for a production-ready version of this code.

