Memory allocation and synchronization mechanism for the octree node structure:
```c++
void allocate(std::unique_ptr<T[]>& ptr, size_t newSize) {
    if (newSize == 0) {
        throw std::invalid_argument("Invalid memory allocation request!");
    }

    T* newArray = nullptr;
    try {
        newArray = new T[newSize];
    } catch(const std::bad_alloc& e){
        throw e;
    }

    if (ptr != nullptr) {
        for (size_t i = 0; i < ptr.get().size() && i < newSize; ++i) {
            newArray[i] = ptr.get()[i];
        }
    }

    std::unique_ptr<T[]> temp(newArray);
    ptr.swap(temp);
}
```
