Creating a connection using Java's NIO library:

```java
import java.io.IOException;
import java.net.InetSocketAddress;
import java.nio.channels.AsynchronousServerSocketChannel;
import java.util.concurrent.ExecutionException;
import java.util.logging.Logger;

public class ConnectionHandler {
    private final AsynchronousServerSocketChannel serverSocketChannel = AsynchronousServerSocketChannel.open();

    public void startListening(String hostname, int port) throws IOException {
        serverSocketChannel.bind(new InetSocketAddress(hostname, port));

        while (true) {
            try {
                serverSocketChannel.accept().get();
                Logger.getGlobal().info("Accepted new connection");
            } catch (InterruptedException | ExecutionException e) {
                Logger.getGlobal().severe(e.toString());
            }
        }
    }
}
```
This code creates a server that listens for incoming connections and accepts them asynchronously.

