For JavaScript part of the task, it can be achieved using following JavaScript function:

```javascript
function copyBytes(chunks, chunkSize, byteCount) {
    let copiedData = Buffer.alloc(byteCount);
    let bytesCopied = 0;

    for (let i=0; i<chunks.length && bytesCopied < byteCount; i++) {
        if (chunkSize !== chunks[i].length) {
            throw new Error(`Chunk ${i} size does not match expectations`);
        }

        let remainingBytes = Math.min(byteCount - bytesCopied, chunkSize);
        chunks[i].copy(copiedData, bytesCopied, 0, remainingBytes);
        bytesCopied += remainingBytes;
    }

    if (bytesCopied < byteCount) {
        throw new Error('Requested byte count exceeds available data');
    }

    return copiedData;
}
```

This function copies a specified number of bytes from an array of buffered data chunks and returns the copied data in a new buffer. It throws an error if chunk sizes do not match expectations or the requested byte count exceeds available data.

